    "result_text": "Stewards can now move a claim to another person on the sheet. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec, and the front end type-checks cleanly.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Who and which claims:** only a steward can move a claim, and only if it is DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING. A move is refused, with the message shown in the claim row's `claim-error`, when:\n  - the user isn't a steward,\n  - the claim is SETTLED or VOID,\n  - no person is chosen, the person doesn't exist, or it's the claim's own person.\n  \n  A refused move writes nothing to the store or the audit file.\n- **What changes:** the claim keeps its number and date. Any figure a statement bound it to is cleared, so its due follows its new person's rate again. Each moved claim is marked `stated: no`.\n- **Totals and audit:** the `CLAIM_REASSIGNED \u2026 from=<old> to=<new>` line is written in the same form as the other claim lines. The ROLLUP and TOTALS lines follow it whenever the move changes a figure.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **New endpoint:** `PUT /api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}/person`, with body `{ personId }`. It's defined in `officefloor/rest/api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}/person.PUT.yml`. I used a separate `PUT` path rather than adding a \"reassign\" action to the existing `POST \u2026/{action}` route, so the two routes can't clash.\n- **New backend classes:** `ValidateReassign`, `ApplyReassign`, `AuditClaimReassigned`, `ReassignRequest` and `Reassignment`.\n- **Stored data:** a claim's person can now be changed (`Claim.setPersonId`), and saving a claim now writes `person_id`. No database migration was needed.\n- **Screen:** each claim row has a `claim-reassign-to` dropdown of the sheet's other people and a `claim-reassign` button. Taking any action on the row clears the old error.\n\nThe request didn't cover a few cases, so the app allows them for now: moving a claim dated in a closed period, and moving a claim to a retired or held person. The dropdown also lists retired people even when they are hidden from the list. Tell me if any of these should be refused.",
